Nuevo Universal Keyboard:

The Dvorak typewriter keyboard letter arrangement is designed for writing using two-hands. That scheme is apposite for writing any language that uses the Latin, Cyrillic or Greek script.

The Post-Mechanical Dvorak 2025 keymap has 48 character keys. This makes it compatible with ISO keyboards.

I have created and tested Windows drivers for several European languages. Linux drivers will be developed next, Apple is not my wheelhouse.

The US English ISO driver was written to facilitate developing European language drivers (the locations of the '[ ]' and '- =' key sets are swapped).

US(English) Post-Mechanical keyboard users should not install the ISO driver, the keyboard is hardwired to use the Microsoft's native US(English) QWERTY driver.

Linux OS users of the US(English) Post-Mechanical also use the native US-QWERTY driver.

Ronald Earl Walker
